From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: update USXGMII rate adaptation on link up

Patch 622 restricted speed-specific PCS programming to forced links,
which unintentionally undid the in-band USXGMII rate-adaptation fix in
patch 620. USXGMII still requires the resolved speed to be applied to
the mode and rate-adaptation registers after link-up.

Run the USXGMII/10GBASE-R speed update for both in-band and out-of-band
phylink modes. Keep forced SGMII and Base-X programming restricted to
out-of-band mode.

This restores the behavior introduced by Ryan Chen in patch 620 while
retaining the later per-port PCS state handling.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -972,6 +972,7 @@
 	struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv = port->priv;
 	const struct airoha_pcs_match_data *data;
 	struct airoha_pcs_maps *maps;
+	int ret = 0;
 
 	maps = &priv->maps[port->index];
 	data = priv->data;
@@ -993,14 +994,11 @@
 				   FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_RATE_ADAPT_RX_AFIFO_RD_THR, 0x5));
 	}
 
-	if (neg_mode != PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED) {
-		int ret = 0;
-
+	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII ||
+	    interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10GBASER) {
+		ret = airoha_pcs_set_usxgmii_speed(maps, speed);
+	} else if (neg_mode != PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED) {
 		switch (interface) {
-		case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII:
-		case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10GBASER:
-			ret = airoha_pcs_set_usxgmii_speed(maps, speed);
-			break;
 		case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII:
 		case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_1000BASEX:
 		case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX:
@@ -1009,13 +1007,13 @@
 		default:
 			break;
 		}
-
-		if (ret)
-			dev_warn_ratelimited(priv->dev,
-					     "unsupported %s speed %d\n",
-					     phy_modes(interface), speed);
 	}
 
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(priv->dev,
+				     "unsupported %s speed %d\n",
+				     phy_modes(interface), speed);
+
 	if (data->link_up)
 		data->link_up(priv, port->index);
 
